  "source_findings": [
    "Exact RP5 two-field secant and temporal precision with public prior-update exploration. Noise amplitude derives only from row predictor/corrector disagreement and deterministic accepted row length; no target/scorer/geometry/horizon.",
    "The Rademacher table is drawn once during accepted corrector finalize, before accepted EMA and precision observation. Previews do not draw it. Scope is actual prior parameters, not post-generation sample correction.",
    "Seed+6 stream is a private generator and appended to instance _STREAMS; generic preview restore, checkpoint save/load validation and exception rollback include it. Sampling rejects the same generator. Full update remains inside serial context.",
    "Two field evaluations per accepted update:1800 accepted updates and3600 native fields across these completed broad gates. Package identity matches the pretraining source lock in both immutable ZIPs.",
    "No deterministic source defect was found in the reviewed declared route. Both complete frozen broader gates fail. No ring or long score is inherited or claimed."
  ],
  "evidence_limitations": [
    "Proposal promises separately hashed new seed6 RNG receipt; broader initial.json files do not emit per-stream hashes. Source and retained checkpoints include the new stream, but this stdlib audit cannot independently prove initial common/private/new RNG tensor hashes from those JSONs. Image global data hash and all1200 tiny-task caller batch/cursor receipts do match.",
    "max_row_noise_to_step is the analytic sqrt(disagreement) bound, not an independently recomputed realized per-row ratio. Aggregate noise_l2 is logged and bounded by deterministic_prior_l2 in every retained step.",
    "Frozen broad tasks cover only unconditional GANTrainer. Factory/custom conditional/auxiliary transaction support, cross-process CUDA replay and horizon-prefix proof remain unqualified.",
    "No Torch import/checkpoint tensor deserialization/model rerun. No shared manifest or research evidence directory edits in this source-only RP9 review."
  ]
